-### Integration Checklist
+## Conclusion
 
-When integrating these components into the application:
+This design document provides comprehensive specifications for implementing the Agent Console with a liquid glass visual language. Every component, animation, and interaction follows the six-layer composition principle to create a living, breathing material system.
 
-- [ ] Replace loading spinners with skeleton screens
-- [ ] Add stagger animations to agent/session lists
-- [ ] Add page transitions to sidebar view switching
-- [ ] Add scroll reveals to message history
-- [ ] Use toggle/checkbox/radio in settings
-- [ ] Add shimmer to premium loading states
-- [ ] Use animated links in navigation
-- [ ] Test all animations at 60fps
-- [ ] Verify reduced motion support
-- [ ] Measure performance impact
+**Key Takeaways:**
 
----
+1. **Glass is a material behavior** - Not just a visual effect
+2. **Six layers are required** - Background, surface, border, content, depth, motion
+3. **Vibrant backgrounds are essential** - Glass needs color to refract
+4. **Accessibility is non-negotiable** - Contrast, reduced motion, reduced transparency
+5. **Performance matters** - Reduce blur on mobile, use containment, optimize animations
 
